From 8a2c945c28f0bbfc996f43351a366e9b60f0999f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Benjamin Millar <benjamin.j.millar@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:59:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ML4 W5/W6: ML4 attention block and router in the rank step,
 G6_MODEL_ML4 only

- attention: FP16 latent row (kvfmt f16ml4, 1152 B), LeRoPE x YaRN frequencies from G.rope_freq (g6a_ml4_rope),
  NoPE layers (indexer no_rope), KV-sharing layers (kv_shared, g6a_ml4_bind_kv_alias; append checks skip them),
  generic mla_scores / context_parts for the FP16 row
- kernels/ml4_glue.cuh: q prep into the core 256-wide layout (ssmax, sqrt 2), indexer LayerNorm and ssmax,
  output compaction to 128 value dims, final logit softcap
- glue: k_router_plan_ml4 (softmax top-4 of 128 + the shared expert as route 4); tests/router_ml4_test.cu
- bind / rank: make_layer_ml4, launch_attn_block_ml4, F16W head; prefill router refuses ML4 (not ported)
- m4sim: GR8_MOE_TOPK check for ML4

Verified: m4sim on the 5-layer subset (0,1,3,35,39) vs an fp32 PyTorch reference: argmax 64/64 at 1, 4, 8 rows;
GLM build: attn.cu SASS identical to the parent commit, m4sim / bind / ops objects identical.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
